{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And I will make your sanctuaries desolate.</b> Even at the hour when they are desolate, they stand in their holiness. And they said in the Midrash Tehillim: Rabbi Pedat said — whether the Temple is destroyed or whether it is not destroyed, the Shekhinah has never departed from within it, as it is said (Psalms 11:4): ״ה' בהיכל קדשו ה' בשמים כסאו״ — even though His throne is in heaven, the Shekhinah is in the Temple, and the sanctuary stands in its holiness, as it is said (I Kings 9:3): ״והיו עיני ולבי שם כל הימים״; and likewise it says (Psalms 3:5): ״ויענני מהר קדשו סלה״ — even though it is a mountain, it stands in its holiness, סלה; and likewise it says (Micah 4:10): ״כי עתה תצאי מקריה ושכנת בשדה״ — and it is written ושכנתי — even though it is destroyed and becomes a field, My Shekhinah is in the field. Rabbi Aḥa said: the Shekhinah never departs from the Western Wall, as it is said (Song of Songs 2:9): ״הנה זה עומד אחר כתלנו״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:50.616742624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}